-## Subtopics
-
-### SDF Sphere Onion
-Applying the onion operation to a sphere creates a spherical shell. This is the most common use case, often used for hollow balls or bubbles. Choose this when a simple hollow sphere is needed. [Link to SDF Sphere](1830-sdf-sphere.md)
-
-### SDF Box Onion
-Applying the onion operation to a box creates a hollow rectangular container. Useful for crates or rooms. Choose this when a hollow box is needed. [Link to SDF Box](1831-sdf-box.md)
-
-### Recursive Onion
-The onion operation can be applied recursively to create multiple concentric shells. This involves nesting onion operations or combining multiple onion SDFs with boolean operations. Choose this for complex layered structures. [Link to SDF Union](1832-sdf-union.md)
